        "content": "<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">instance</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">AddZeroClass</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">MulZeroClass</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">PartialOrder</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">CanonicallyOrderedAdd</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">PosMulReflectLE</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IsLeftCancelMulZero</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">mul_left_cancel_of_ne_zero</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">mul_left_cancel_iff_of_pos</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h0</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">pos</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">|&gt;.</span><span class=\"n\">mp</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>This instance fails because both <code>AddZeroClass</code> and <code>MulZeroClass</code> provide a <code>Zero</code>.<br>\nShould we create <code>AddMulZeroClass</code>? Or perhaps <code>IsAddZeroClass</code>/<code>IsMulZeroClass</code>?</p>",
        "id": 579416606,
        "sender_full_name": "Snir Broshi",
        "timestamp": 1773475934
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Alternatively you could use <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=NonUnitalNonAssocSemiring#doc\">docs#NonUnitalNonAssocSemiring</a> which seems to be the LCM of both typeclasses</p>",
        "id": 579515565,
        "sender_full_name": "Violeta Hernández",
        "timestamp": 1773554742
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Yes but ordinals don't satisfy that :(</p>",
        "id": 579515610,
        "sender_full_name": "Snir Broshi",
        "timestamp": 1773554782
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>If you only want this for ordinals it might be easiest to just inline the proof in the ordinal instance</p>",
        "id": 579515966,
        "sender_full_name": "Violeta Hernández",
        "timestamp": 1773555036
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Yeah but that's not general, very non-Mathlib-y</p>",
        "id": 579515989,
        "sender_full_name": "Snir Broshi",
        "timestamp": 1773555059
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Ordinals hold a weird position as \"the closest thing to a ring that we care about, that doesn't even satisfy the weakest ring axioms.\" I'm not aware of anything else in Mathlib in this position. I don't think the generality gives us much.</p>",
        "id": 579516662,
        "sender_full_name": "Violeta Hernández",
        "timestamp": 1773555641
    },
